{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":"The mobile overlay uses"}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":" `fixed inset-0` with"}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":" `z-40`. The header "}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":"bar uses `relative z-50`."}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":" This creates a stacking"}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":" context issue. The "}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":"bar may not appear above"}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":" the overlay."}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":"\n\nThe overlay is a child"}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":" of the sticky header,"}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":" so it shares the header's"}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":" stacking context. The"}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":" bar and menu buttons"}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":" sit at z-50, above "}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":"the overlay's z-40. "}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":"This keeps the button"}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":" clickable. The overlay"}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":" will only cover content painted below the header"}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":" in the root stacking"}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":" context.\n\nSticky headers do "}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":"not contain fixed positioning."}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":" The overlay competes"}
{"type":"assistant-thought","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":" with other page elements for z-index. The entire header stacking context may overlap unrelated content.\n\nThe overlay will not dim the header bar. The bar sits above the overlay, so the white background covers only the bar area. Clicking the dimmed space closes the menu. The bar area remains undimmed, which is standard behavior.\n\nLocalhostHeader is the correct component to modify. The hamburger menu has been added."}
{"type":"assistant-text","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","text":"The hamburger menu was already sketched in, but it wasn’t usable on small screens. Here’s what was wrong and what changed:\n\n1. **Desktop nav stayed visible** on mobile — it now hides below 800px (`mq800:hidden`)\n2. **Wrong breakpoints** — this project uses `mq800`, not `md:`\n3. **Stacking** — the overlay no longer blocks the menu button; the icon toggles to an X when open\n\nOn viewports ≤800px you’ll get the hamburger; larger screens keep the desktop links."}
{"type":"turn-completed","turnId":"7e7569df-151f-4fcf-87b9-d0b7695174c3","stopReason":"end_turn"}
